A1: usertrap() called syscall()

A2: The value is 0xf (decimal 15). This represents system call number 15, which is SYS_open - the system call to open
a file.

A3: The previous mode was User mode. This is determined by the SPP (Supervisor Previous Privilege) bit in the 
sstatus register (0x200000022) being 0 which is the 8th bit.

A4: The assembly instruction is lw a5,0(zero). Register a5 corresponds to the variable num.

A5: The kernel crashes because it attempts to read from memory address 0 as in bugged instruction (*(int *) 0).
Address 0 is not mapped in the kernel's address space, this causes a load page fault, indicated by scause=0xd.
The faulting address is given by stval=0x0.
